WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.801
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)
-Hi, CNN.

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.169
We've missed you
these last five months.

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.303
Great to be back.

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:07.239
I'm here with editor-at-large
of<i> Reason</i> magazine, Matt Welch,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.642
and senior editor
for<i> The Dispatch</i> , Sarah Isgur.

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:12.778
Okay, Sarah. "Which one
of the Trump indictments

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.447
do you think is the strongest?"

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.182
Oh, there's so many
to choose from.

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:17.950
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.585
But it's a really easy question.

00:00:19.718 --> 00:00:22.155
It's the Florida case about
the classified documents

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.289
in the obstruction side.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.257
You'll notice Trump
and his allies never talk

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:26.392
about that one.

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:28.428
The other cases
are all much weaker

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.430
in a variety of ways,
but that Florida case...

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:33.032
So, this is the one where
he took classified documents

00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:35.034
-and put them by the toilet.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:36.569
-(BILL MAHER LAUGHING)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.938
-You know--
-Why is that such a strong case?

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:41.407
It's after he's president.

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:44.977 line:0%
There's just no real
legal defense to, you know,

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:46.445 line:0%
even if you're
really constipated,

00:00:46.578 --> 00:00:48.214 line:0%
needing those documents
by your toilet...

00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:52.352 line:0%
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)
-(LAUGHS) But...

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:56.589
I know what they're gonna say,
which is,

00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:59.992
"Biden did the same thing,
he had papers by his Corvette."

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:01.594
He didn't defy a subpoena

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:02.862
-and then he lied about it.
-BILL: That's true.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:03.930
I know that. I'm just saying.

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.298
He's not charged
with having the documents

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:07.166
or taking the documents,
he's charged with not giving

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.901
the documents back
when the government was like,

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:10.836
-knock knock, "Can we have
our documents back?"
-BILL: Right.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:11.971
-And see...
-"What documents?"

00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:13.739
...this is what I mean
when I always say,

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:17.977
-he's stupid and crazy.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:20.246
They're... (LAUGHS)

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.549
They're stupid like I think

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.351
Frederick Douglass
is still alive.

00:01:25.484 --> 00:01:27.954
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.756
The stealth bomber
is literally invisible,

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:34.393
you know, healthcare is,
no one knew it was complicated.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.828
-Those are stupid.
-(AUDIENCE MEMBER LAUGHING)

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:39.031
Crazy is this. It's just crazy.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.500
It's just a crazy,
unforced error.

00:01:41.633 --> 00:01:44.036
Why do it?
He wasn't even looking at them.

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:46.372
It just was... "They're mine."

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:50.476
-Yeah? That...
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:52.945
And then when they came
and asked for the documents,

00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:54.480
and he said no,

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.081
and then they tried
to move the documents,

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:57.417
then he realized
that was on camera

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.318
and so then he told the guy
to flood the server...

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:02.822
-I mean it was like, every step.
-(BILL LAUGHING) Okay.

00:02:03.622 --> 00:02:06.192
"Nikki Haley rose
in the polls this week."

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:10.229
-Oh, good for you.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.131
Nine to ten percent. Nailing it.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:14.934
-(LAUGHS) Is that what it is?
-(SARAH ISGUR CHUCKLES)

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:16.769
"Are there enough
establishing voters

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:21.441
in the Republican party for her
to become a serious revival,

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.008
revival to Trump?"

00:02:23.475 --> 00:02:24.677
-"Revival?"
-(MATT WELCH) Rival. Rival.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.646
-Rival.
-BILL: Rival. Oh, okay.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:29.481
Well, we're doing this
on the fly, you know.

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:31.551
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-Rival to Trump, yes.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:34.287
-Oh, hell no.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.989
-(BILL LAUGHS) Okay. No?
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:02:37.122 --> 00:02:39.258
There's actually
a really interesting poll,

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:41.761 line:0%
I recommend people look
at the people at fair vote

00:02:42.294 --> 00:02:43.395 line:0%
who do ranked-choice voting.

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:47.400 line:0%
They had a poll that basically
did ranked-choice

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:49.468 line:0%
with the candidates,
a national poll,

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.871
and so each time around
you kick someone off the island

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:55.475
and then see how it goes
until you get to only two left.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.343
And Donald Trump got
like 47 percent or something

00:02:58.477 --> 00:02:59.846
in the first vote, first round.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.447
And then, you know,
Doug Burgum goes

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.182
and Mike Pence goes,
bop, bop, bop, bop, bop.

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:04.850
He doesn't go up
even a little bit.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:07.986
Turns out 47 percent
of Republicans really want

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.622
Donald Trump
to be the president,

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:12.625
and he was also number 13 by...
(CHUCKLES) ...the most people.

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:14.160
-(BILL LAUGHS) Oh.
-Like, he was last place.

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:16.028
Like, please anybody
but Donald Trump.

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:17.530
He only, like,
gets over the majority

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:19.332
when everybody else
is wiped out.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:20.767
Nikki Haley does very well
in that poll.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:21.900
She comes in second

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:23.936
once you start
knocking off Chris Christie,

00:03:24.069 --> 00:03:26.138
and all these
semi-establishment people.

00:03:26.605 --> 00:03:30.076
She will, she has the ability
maybe to look,

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.211
to get some people
who want to vote for Trump,

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:35.814
but the only way to get to
the Republican nomination is--

00:03:35.948 --> 00:03:37.750
and this is why Ron DeSantis
still has a chance,

00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:39.552
although he's
absolutely nosedived

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.020
during this calendar year,

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:42.988
is that people
who like Ron DeSantis

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.424
also like
Donald Trump sometimes.

00:03:45.557 --> 00:03:46.692
He can straddle that.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.895
Nikki Haley hasn't
quite shown that,

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.062
and the rest of them
have no chance.

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:52.098
She has really been
across the board, though.

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:55.034
I remember when the rumor was
that they were having an affair.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:56.368
-(SARAH CHUCKLES)
-Remember that?

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.404
It was in the first Trump book.

00:03:58.537 --> 00:03:59.872
-Do you remember that?
-SARAH: Yeah, I mean--

00:04:00.005 --> 00:04:01.173
-No, I didn't
ever believe it either...
-(CHUCKLES)

00:04:01.306 --> 00:04:03.675
...but she's gone from that
to I wouldn't even have her

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:04.810
on the ticket.

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:07.313
Look, I worked
for Carly Fiorina in 2016

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:08.681
and we're seeing
the exact same problem

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:09.815
that we saw then.

00:04:09.948 --> 00:04:11.651
You can't have this
many candidates in the field.

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:13.485
-That poll,
which was fascinating...
-Yeah.

00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:15.654
...actually showed in the end
that Ron DeSantis

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.923
could beat Donald Trump
by three points.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.126
If it were only
the two of them in the race.

00:04:20.292 --> 00:04:23.429
Right. Well, okay,
so was anyone surprised

00:04:23.562 --> 00:04:25.898
that Donald Trump...
(SIGHS) Boy...

00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:27.333
-MATT: No.
-...it's hard to... (LAUGHS)

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.535
-(LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:32.004
-SARAH: Next question.
Next question.
-(LAUGHS)

00:04:32.137 --> 00:04:36.408
-Keep going. (LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.543
Wait a second.

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.878
"Leaked intel." Oh, I read this.

00:04:40.012 --> 00:04:42.347
"On our nuclear
submarine program

00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:44.483
to an Australian businessman."

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:48.387
You know what, I'm the last guy
to defend Trump.

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:52.358
This sounds like BS to me.
I mean, he, of course,

00:04:52.491 --> 00:04:54.860
he does a million things
that you shouldn't do,

00:04:54.993 --> 00:04:57.196
but leaked intel on
our nuclear submarine program.

00:04:57.329 --> 00:04:58.831
I doubt if he knows
the first thing

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:00.099
-about our nuclear su--
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:05:00.232 --> 00:05:01.934
-And I--
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:05.071
You know, I don't think
he gave away technical secrets,

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:07.340
which he was just bragging,
you know, "Our submarines."

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.742
And I'm kind of glad
that it gets around the world

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:11.243
that we can kick your ass.

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:12.678
(BOTH LAUGH)

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.180
This is the problem
where you think Trump

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:16.848
is like evil and stupid, like,
it's kind of one of the other.

00:05:16.982 --> 00:05:18.284
-Like he's an evil genius.
-No. Crazy and stupid.

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:20.018
Not yours, I'm just saying
other people.

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:21.921
Like, you can't believe
he's like the super genius

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:23.489
who knows everything about
our nuclear subs,

00:05:23.622 --> 00:05:25.090
-but also...
-Right. (LAUGHS) Right.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:27.025
...he's a moron
who like doesn't know...

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:28.327
-Right, exactly.
-...like left and right are.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:31.263
-It can't be both.
-Right. Okay, all right.

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:34.233
-"What is the--"
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:38.371
"What is the panel think
of California Governor Newsom

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:42.808
repealing the law that
banned doctors from sharing

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:46.545
unapproved COVID information?"
Well, of course, I love it.

00:05:46.912 --> 00:05:49.381
They should have never done
in the first place.

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:50.883
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:53.586
Doctors should be able
to speak freely.

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:58.323
The media should be
the watchdog of what's going on

00:05:58.457 --> 00:06:00.459
in the government,
not the megaphone,

00:06:00.592 --> 00:06:03.195
not the amplifier of it.

00:06:03.328 --> 00:06:04.596
I can't believe
you brought up this case,

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.799
'cause I'm really obsessed
with this idea that Newsom

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:09.468
and DeSantis are actually,
you know, different sides

00:06:09.601 --> 00:06:11.803
of the same coin when it comes
to civil liberties,

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:13.038
-like free speech.
-BILL: Right.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:14.874
Newsom is banning doctors
from saying something

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:17.076
about COVID that he doesn't
personally believe to.

00:06:17.209 --> 00:06:18.911 line:0%
-BILL: Well, now he's not.
-Okay, well,

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:21.613 line:0%
Corden joined him first,
so, you know, okay.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.516 line:0%
And at the same time, you know,
DeSantis down in Florida,

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.285 line:0%
is telling teachers
that they can't, you know,

00:06:26.418 --> 00:06:27.586 line:0%
teach certain things
at universities.

00:06:27.719 --> 00:06:29.521
Like, how about just
the First Amendment?

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:31.624
-I'm pro that.
-BILL: Yeah.

00:06:31.757 --> 00:06:33.626
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)
-MATT: I also say that--

00:06:35.961 --> 00:06:38.897
Gavin Newsom wanting to run
for president is the best thing

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.399
that could happen
to Californians.

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:41.534
(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:43.569
'Cause he'll make
a better governor that way.

00:06:44.136 --> 00:06:45.404
-I'd say the same thing.
-MATT: Yeah.

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:46.772
I think he's a great politician.

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:48.240
I've been trying to get him
to run for president

00:06:48.373 --> 00:06:49.242
-for 15 years.
-(MATT LAUGHS)

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:52.378
It would force him to go to the
center like this kind of stuff.

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:54.279
And that brief
I mentioned at the Supreme Court

00:06:54.413 --> 00:06:56.815
right now wants to, like, have
a different homeless policy.

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.817
Like, he's moving to the center
on all sorts of stuff.

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:00.185
And he can win. You know what?

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:02.288
It doesn't hurt
to have a dreamy candidate.

00:07:02.421 --> 00:07:06.225
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)
-I'm not-- I feel it doesn't.

00:07:06.359 --> 00:07:08.227
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)
-I'm sorry.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.362
I don't know.
That bear skin rug photo,

00:07:10.495 --> 00:07:11.630
like, really weirds me out.

00:07:11.763 --> 00:07:13.599
-BILL: The what?
-The-- (LAUGHS)

00:07:13.732 --> 00:07:15.901
-BILL: What photo?
-The photo with him...

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:17.536
-MATT: Kimberly Guilfoyle.
-...and Kimberly Guilfoyle

00:07:17.669 --> 00:07:19.237
where he's like
on the bear skin rug

00:07:19.371 --> 00:07:21.039
and it's like really--
I don't know. Not my type.

00:07:21.173 --> 00:07:22.207
-What can I say?
-BILL: All right.

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:23.542
-(LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:26.845
"Should the Senate have loosened
the dress code to allow

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:30.049
for John Fetterman's shorts
and casual attire?"

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:33.652
-No. This--
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:36.021
That-- I mean,
that was so ridiculous.

00:07:37.055 --> 00:07:40.926
I mean, I can't-- What is this
with John Fetterman?

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.060
Come on, man.

00:07:42.294 --> 00:07:44.931
If you haven't seen it,
he looks like Kevin Smith.

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:46.932
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-Remember Kevin's,

00:07:47.066 --> 00:07:49.602
the hockey shorts in the Senate?

00:07:49.735 --> 00:07:50.736
I mean, what is it?

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:53.472
What point is this making?
What is the point of this?

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:54.773
I never got it.

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:59.678
I'm so torn between my hatred
of rules and institutions...

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:02.047
-(BILL LAUGHS)
-...and my hatred

00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:04.116
of inappropriate--
or people who dress like me

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:06.051
on weekends being in the Senate?

00:08:06.185 --> 00:08:08.554
That's bad. We don't want people
who look like me.

00:08:08.687 --> 00:08:10.089
I know. I just feel
it was such a stunt.

00:08:10.222 --> 00:08:11.890
It's like, oh,
I'm the man of the people.

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:12.892
But you know what?

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:14.727
You know what
the people actually have to do?

00:08:15.161 --> 00:08:16.428
-Dress.
-Yeah, for work.

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:18.930
Yeah. Dress for work. All right.

00:08:19.064 --> 00:08:20.932
It gives you
some of that luxury good stuff.

00:08:21.066 --> 00:08:23.268
This idea that you're a man
of the people.

00:08:23.402 --> 00:08:25.371
-He comes from an incredibly
privileged background.
-BILL: Right.

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:28.006
He's never, like,
been faced with being fired

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.742
for not wearing something right
to work and then,

00:08:29.875 --> 00:08:31.010
-you know, that's what you get.
-BILL: Well...

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.079
The people who are always going
on about privilege

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:35.547
always have the privilege
to be impractical

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:37.216
-in every possible way.
-(SARAH CHUCKLES)

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:40.185
But we gotta go. Thank you, CNN.
We'll see you next week.

00:08:40.319 --> 00:08:43.456
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING, CHEERING)

